New: The 'gravity calculation' postprocessor can now include the
gravitational contribution of the mass associated with the dynamic
topography of the top and bottom boundaries. The topography is taken from
the 'dynamic topography' postprocessor and treated as a thin sheet of mass,
which makes it possible to compute complete gravity anomalies for models
with free-slip boundaries, including regional chunk models. The new
parameters are 'Include surface topography contribution' and 'Include
bottom topography contribution'.
<br>
(Bernard Che Ngu, 2026/10/23)
